--TEST--
`+`, `-` and `~` agree on refusing every operand `rule:types/arithmetic` has no row for, and an object gets the one sentence the others do not — `rule:types/conversion` and `rule:types/arithmetic`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Thing {
    public int $n = 1;
}

string $s = "5";
bool $b = true;
array<int> $xs = [1, 2];
Thing $o = new Thing();

// PHP answers each of these by converting the operand first — `+"5"` is
// `5`, `-true` is `-1`, `~"ab"` is a bytewise NOT. `rule:types/conversion` has no
// implicit conversion for any of them to be, so all three prefixes refuse,
// and they refuse *alike*: the asserted property is that the three agree,
// not that any one of them reports.
string $s1 = +$s;
string $s2 = -$s;
string $s3 = ~$s;

// The same answer one domain over. `bool` is where PHP's conversion is
// least visible and Novis's refusal most valuable — `-true` reads as if it
// meant something.
bool $b1 = -$b;

// An `array<T>` reaches the same refusal rather than a per-element one.
array<int> $q = ~$xs;

// An object parts from them: Novis has no operator overloading, so the
// sentence that author needs is "call the member that does this", not
// "convert it first". Same operand position, different diagnostic.
Thing $o1 = -$o;

echo $s1, $s2, $s3, $b1;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0705]: `+` has no meaning for `string`
   --> %s:16:14
   |
16 | string $s1 = +$s;
   |              ^^^ a unary arithmetic operator is over numbers
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP converts this operand first and Novis never converts by itself, so say it — `$x as int`

error[E0705]: `-` has no meaning for `string`
   --> %s:17:14
   |
17 | string $s2 = -$s;
   |              ^^^ a unary arithmetic operator is over numbers
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP converts this operand first and Novis never converts by itself, so say it — `$x as int`

error[E0705]: `~` has no meaning for `string`
   --> %s:18:14
   |
18 | string $s3 = ~$s;
   |              ^^^ a unary arithmetic operator is over numbers
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP converts this operand first and Novis never converts by itself, so say it — `$x as int`

error[E0705]: `-` has no meaning for `bool`
   --> %s:23:12
   |
23 | bool $b1 = -$b;
   |            ^^^ a unary arithmetic operator is over numbers
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP converts this operand first and Novis never converts by itself, so say it — `$x as int`

error[E0705]: `~` has no meaning for `array<int>`
   --> %s:26:17
   |
26 | array<int> $q = ~$xs;
   |                 ^^^^ a unary arithmetic operator is over numbers
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP converts this operand first and Novis never converts by itself, so say it — `$x as int`

error[E0401]: `-` has no meaning for `Thing`
   --> %s:31:13
   |
31 | Thing $o1 = -$o;
   |             ^^^ an object takes part in no arithmetic
   = help: Novis has no operator overloading; call the member that does this — a `Core\Time\Duration` negates with `->negated()` and subtracts with `->minus(…)`

